  "version": null,
  "vision": "The .hecksagon language, declared in itself. A hecksagon is a SIBLING of a bluebook, not part of one — it binds a domain's aggregates to the ports/adapters that carry them, and those bindings belong to the deployment's wiring rather than to the domain's own rules. So it is described in its own file, as its own thing, the same reasoning world.bluebook already carries for .world."
